<title>RUSSIA: Russian oil firm ONAKO raises crude output in 1996.</title>
<headline>Russian oil firm ONAKO raises crude output in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian oil company Orenburgskaya Neftyanaya Aktsionernaya Kompaniya (ONAKO) produced 7.89 million tonnes of oil in 1996, up from 7.58 million in 1995, the company said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said proven oil reserves stood at 281.36 million tonnes.</p>
<p>ONAKO is one of around a dozen vertically-integrated Russian oil groups created over the last few years. Its main operating unit is Orenburgneft.</p>
<p>ONAKO gave the following figures for 1996 (in millions of tonnes) --</p>
<p>					     1996		1995</p>
<p>Oil output				 7.89		7.58</p>
<p>Refined oil				4.45		4.39</p>
<p>Oil exports				2.17		1.95</p>
<p>(to all destinations, including in the Commonwealth of Independent States)</p>
<p>--Mike Collett-White, Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8052</p>
</text>
